From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: =?UTF-8?q?Lu=C3=ADs=20Duarte?= <lduarte@cloudflare.com>
Date: Mon, 12 Oct 2026 11:07:13 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] ast: box the large, rarely used expression and statement
 variants

An enum is as large as its largest variant, so the inline function
expressions and tagged templates made every Expression 128 bytes on
wasm32, and for-in/for-of, switch and try made every Statement 312.
Most nodes are identifiers, calls and member accesses. Boxing the big
variants brings Expression to 48 and Statement to 64 bytes and halves a
bundle's syntax tree, at one extra allocation per function expression.
